From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:22:06 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] DevTools: no frontend on Windows 10 Mobile

The phone browser has no DevTools window, and the frontend is a TypeScript
bundle built with node and esbuild. enable_devtools_frontend is already
false on iOS and Fuchsia, so content builds without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 content/browser/devtools/features.gni | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/features.gni b/content/browser/devtools/features.gni
index 24c49b5bd6007ca4f2b7790d93860e7f52317ef8..dded7a65880265356edd8cff5066e75238041594 100644
--- a/content/browser/devtools/features.gni
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/features.gni
@@ -5,4 +5,8 @@
 import("//build/config/chrome_build.gni")
 
 # iOS and Fuchsia don't support DevTools front-end.
-enable_devtools_frontend = !is_ios && !is_fuchsia
+import("//build/config/win/w10m.gni")
+
+# Not on Windows 10 Mobile either: the phone browser has no DevTools window,
+# and the frontend is a TypeScript build (node, esbuild) of its own.
+enable_devtools_frontend = !is_ios && !is_fuchsia && !is_w10m
